Why: cscc/ilrun shortcut; the remaining cscc errors in mono-2.6.4's 
basic-profile corlib.  (1) MethodCall/MethodResponse/ReturnMessage: cscc 
does not accept the public read/write Uri property as the implementation of 
the get-only IMethodMessage.Uri; add the explicit implementation, as Guix' 
mono-1.2.6-bootstrap.patch does (basic profile only).  (2) 
String.Concat(string,string): two sibling 'fixed' statements declare 
dest/src; cscc puts fixed variables into the enclosing scope ('dest is 
already declared').  Brace each statement (valid C# for every compiler).

diff --git a/mcs/class/corlib/System.Runtime.Remoting.Messaging/MethodCall.cs b/mcs/class/corlib/System.Runtime.Remoting.Messaging/MethodCall.cs
index d925c7e9..b9f94e65 100644
--- a/mcs/class/corlib/System.Runtime.Remoting.Messaging/MethodCall.cs
+++ b/mcs/class/corlib/System.Runtime.Remoting.Messaging/MethodCall.cs
@@ -272,6 +272,14 @@ namespace System.Runtime.Remoting.Messaging {
 			set { _uri = value; }
 		}
 
+#if BOOTSTRAP_WITH_OLDLIB
+		// cscc does not match the public Uri {get;set;} property against
+		// the get-only IMethodMessage.Uri (Guix mono-1.2.6-bootstrap.patch)
+		string IMethodMessage.Uri {
+			get { return Uri; }
+		}
+#endif
+
 		string IInternalMessage.Uri {
 			get { return Uri; }
 			set { Uri = value; }
